  "description": "LAFLAI crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C4 H12 N2 2+,H24 Cr2 Er4 O40 S6 2-,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.910-4.460 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.42-145.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (pipzH2)[Cr2Er4(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)4(H2O)10(μ3-SO4)4(SO4)2]·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Cr(III), Er(III).",
